<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian treasury raises 50 mln dinars at auction.</title>
<headline>Tunisian treasury raises 50 mln dinars at auction.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Treasury on Tuesday raised 50 million dinars at its weekly auction of treasury bills dated May 13, and repaid maturing paper totalling 12.6 million dinars.</p>
<p>It sold five-year notes payable at maturity at a 7.2500 percent coupon rate worth 50 million dinars.</p>
<p>Last time the treasury sold five-year notes was in July at an average 9.4375 percent coupon rate.</p>
<p>Banks bid for 123.2 million dinars for five-year notes at between 7.2500 and 8.1250 percent. (one $=1.08 dinar)</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
